<title>USA: U.S. DAP prices steady in quiet holiday-type trade.</title>
<headline>U.S. DAP prices steady in quiet holiday-type trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. cash diammonium phosphate prices were steady Friday in very quiet dealings, cash sources said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's slow in front of the holiday and deer hunting season has opened and taken many dealers out of the market,&quot; one source said.</p>
<p>The DAP market was underpinned by reports of some export business with China, but the business was not large enough to move prices higher, a trade source said.</p>
<p>Ammonia prices were down on a drop in demand from Midwest producers, dealers said.</p>
<p>			   Dlrs/short ton	Chg from Wednesday</p>
<p>DAP central Fla	   180-182			unc</p>
<p>DAP central La Gulf     188-190			unc</p>
<p>Ammonia/La Gulf	    225			   dn 3-5</p>
